Jukka Lahtinen <jukkal@despammed.com> writes:
> robin <usenet@unrated.net> writes:
> 
> [about the logmoves patch]
> 
> > This patch would allow us to do a "Fastest Ascension" trophy, but
> > only in terms of gametime. It's been suggested that a matching
> > trophy for realtime would also be good.  Would it be particularly
> > difficult to get the logfile to store yyyymmddhhmmss, instead of
> > just yyyymmdd?
> 
> You would probably need to change the toptenentry struct defined at about
> line 43 of topten.c. It now stores deathdate and birthdate as long, and
> the value is the numerical value you see in the logfile. Then you would
> need to update all references to it. Probably not particularly difficult,
> but..

The only trouble there is that yyyymmddhhmmss would break a 32-bit
long, which tops out at 2147483647 (or 4294967295 if you made it
unsigned). You'd need to keep (birth|death)date separate from
(birth|death)time, I think, and expand the struct. (Alternatively,
just store the time_t raw.)

